 "insight": [
  "Luxembourg's exports index in 2025 was 106, the lowest growth among the eight countries compared, with Belgium, the Netherlands, Germany, France, Austria, Spain, and Italy all showing higher indices.",
  "The Netherlands had the highest exports index at 268 in 2025, followed by Spain at 255 and Germany at 200.",
  "Luxembourg's exports index reached its lowest point in 2020 at 79 and its highest in 2006 at 119, showing less growth compared to the other countries whose highest indices were in the 200s.",
  "Luxembourg had the highest intra-EU share of exports at 83.1% in 2025, despite a decline of 6.2 percentage points since 2005, while all other countries also saw decreases in their intra-EU export shares.",
  "The data are in current euros and are not adjusted for price changes, which may affect comparisons over time."
